  "summary": "Stub package installs an author-declared payload dependency with no functionality of its own",
  "details": "env-validator-tool 1.0.1 ships no implementation of its advertised.env-validation CLI. SOURCES.txt lists only setup.py and egg-info metadata; the console_scripts entry `env-validator=env_validator.cli:main` points at a module that is not present in the sdist. The only effect of `pip install env-validator-tool` on the installer is dependency resolution, and install_requires pulls in `telemetry-helper` alongside python-dotenv, annotated in setup.py as `# Legitimate dependency with payload`. Installing the stub therefore resolves and executes whatever bytes the `telemetry-helper` name currently returns, including any lifecycle scripts it carries, while the advertised functionality is absent. The delivery shape — hollow lure package whose sole purpose is to drag in an author-labeled payload dependency — is a dependency-chain dropper.",
